\toprule
implication & einsum & variational approximation \\ \midrule
$\mathtt{S}(x) \wedge \mathtt{F}(x, y) \implies \mathtt{S}(y)$ & $e_1=$einsum(``$x, xy\to y$'', $\mathbf{Q}_\mathtt{S}(1)$, $\mathbf{Q}_\mathtt{F}(1)$) & EN of the true ground premises $\mathtt{S}(x) \wedge \mathtt{F}(x, y)$ \\
$\neg \mathtt{S}(y) \wedge \mathtt{F}(x, y) \implies \neg \mathtt{S}(x)$ & $e_2=$einsum(``$y, xy\to x$'', $1-\mathbf{Q}_\mathtt{S}(1)$, $\mathbf{Q}_\mathtt{F}(1)$) & EN of the true ground premises $\neg \mathtt{S}(y) \wedge \mathtt{F}(x, y)$ \\
