$\DRTO$, a subset of $\DR$, indicates cases where Petri nets detect only the final incorrect transition. Since the timing of this check varies by case, a high $\DRTO$ often implies longer error detection latency. The latency, $\LATENCY$, is calculated excluding detections counted in $\DRTO$.
