The GD metric indicates that RNSGA2 is the best-performing algorithm for this problem. However, when evaluated using the IGD metric, SPEA2 and NSGA2 emerge as the most effective algorithms. This discrepancy highlights the multifaceted nature of evaluating MOEAs and emphasizes the importance of using diverse performance metrics to capture different aspects of algorithmic behavior. By employing multiple metrics on the MORL benchmark, we gain a broader perspective on the performance of MOEAs, enabling a more comprehensive characterization of their strengths and limitations.

A notable observation from the IGD analysis for other problems (figures in Section~4 of the Supplementary Material) is the high efficiency of the PSO algorithm according to this metric. This suggests that PSO can effectively learn a good approximation of the true PF in some scenarios.

