\section{Method}
In this section, we present an overview of the proposed SmartThinker. As shown in Fig. \ref{SmartThinker}, SmartThinker consists of two stages: (i) \textbf{Short-Reasoning Mode Warm-up}, where we adapt a reasoning model to a short-reasoning mode by rejection sampling and SFT, and (ii) \textbf{RL with SCPO}, where the model is trained to impose stronger penalty on redundant steps while relaxing length constraints on critical ones.

