\subsection{Datasets}
\noindent\textbf{Datasets for Low-light Synthesis.} We utilize a combination of the ImageNet \cite{deng2009imagenet} and COCO \cite{lin2014microsoft} datasets, comprising nearly ten million images, as normal-light references for synthesizing low-light images. To improve simulation efficiency and image quality, we first resize and downscale the images by a factor of two, considering the varying quality and high resolutions within these datasets. Subsequently, we randomly crop image patches of size $156 \times 156 \times 3$ for simulation.
