\forall \overline{\phi}$.
\end{lemma}

Thus $U_1(\phi_{END})<U_1(\overline{\phi})$, for all $\overline{\phi}$ with $\overline{\phi}_1^v<1$.
Group 1's individual utility is lowest when its group size is 1, which is a lower bound of any Nash equilibrium.

